illed-trades-scholarship-now-covers-tuition-tools-and-living-costs-as-she-trains-for-an-hvac-career/articleshow/134419301.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/a-canadian-student-expected-to-work-four-or-five-shifts-a-week-to-afford-college-a-20000-skilled-trades-scholarship-now-covers-tuition-tools-and-living-costs-as-she-trains-for-an-hvac-career/articleshow/134419301.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-23T17:03:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134419452,imgsize-461478.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Fabergé figure bought in 1934 resurfaces in New York attic 79 years later, sells for $5.2 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134432375.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After being lost to time, a stunning Fabergé figurine depicting a bodyguard to Empress Alexandra Feodorovna has emerged from an attic in Rhinebeck, New York. Fetching an impressive $5.2 million at auction, this piece, originally commissioned by Emperor Nicholas II, epitomizes the exquisite craftsmanship of the early 20th century, setting a record for Fabergé hardstone figures and reflecting a renewed fascination with imperial Russian artistry.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1934-a-new-york-collector-bought-a-faberg-figure-tied-to-russias-imperial-court-nearly-80-years-later-it-resurfaced-in-a-family-attic-and-sold-at-auction-for-a-record-5-2-million/articleshow/134432375.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1934-a-new-york-collector-bought-a-faberg-figure-tied-to-russias-imperial-court-nearly-80-years-later-it-resurfaced-in-a-family-attic-and-sold-at-auction-for-a-record-5-2-million/articleshow/134432375.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-0